{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Dp8pVxKGwiYd9NGCXd5kEs","type":"tool_result","content":"618:----\n624:----\n625:== .ard/triage/engineer/prompt.txt\n631:== .ard/triage/lead/prompt.txt\n637:== .ard/workers/engineer/prompt.txt\n643:== .ard/reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\n- **Issue body, fixed text** (a test asserts it): treat the credential as leaked and rotate it first; do not add `ard:pending` before the credential is rotated, because triage and worker agents would read the file; and the human runbook (rotate first, remove the value from HEAD, do not close while the secret is still at HEAD, false positives, the cap, history is not rewritten).\n- **Licence:** TruffleHog is AGPL-3.0. It stays out of the published `ard` image (no root `Dockerfile` pin). The binary comes from the role's own Dockerfile, built locally by the operator, or a host install. The role's docs record the licence.\n- **Fails closed** with no \"finished scanning\" summary, nothing scanned, or a count mismatch, so autoclose never closes on a broken scan.\n- **Tests:** a fake trufflehog binary, a canary test over the full field list (a planted fake secret must never appear in stdout, logs or the issue body), fail-closed cases, argv with and without the flags, `exclude-paths` and `allow`, a missing tool exiting 2, and the starter listing tests.\n\n**Done when**\n- [ ] Tests with a fake `trufflehog` binary (no network): one finding per value with all files; lowest detector name; byte-identical output; fingerprint golden; output passes `scanner.DecodeFindings`, every path passes `checkFilePath`, and `redact.Builtin()` finds nothing in it\n- [ ] Canary test: a unique marker in every non-allowlisted field (`Raw`, `RawV2`, `Redacted`, `SecretParts`, `ExtraData`, `StructuredData`, `VerificationError`, `email`, `repository`, `repository_local_path`, `DetectorDescription`) appears nowhere in stdout, stderr or the temp dir, including after a run killed mid-stream\n- [ ] Each fail-closed case exits non-zero with empty stdout; recorded argv contains `--no-verification --no-update --no-ignore-tag --fail-on-scan-errors --json` and none of the forbidden flags\n- [ ] `exclude-paths` and `allow` work; a bad `allow` entry fails the run; a missing tool exits 2\n- [ ] The issue body contains the do-not-re-route sentence and the runbook (test)\n- [ ] The starter tree and `ard config check` accept the role with `route: needs-human`; `ard init` proposes it with `scan` committed as 0755 and the opt-out note in the PR body\n- [ ] The role's docs record the AGPL-3.0 licence and that the binary is not in the `ard` image\n\n**Design:** #203 · **Depends on:** #215 · **Part of:** #203\n\n## Implementation plan\n\nChecked against `origin/main` at e488a54 (2026-11-23). Inputs: #203 (body and owner decisions), `.ard/203/triage-engineer.md` (the three-way split), #215, #217, the tech-lead and PM notes on #203, and the code in `internal/roles`, `internal/scanner`, `internal/redact`, `internal/config`, `internal/initcmd` and `internal/worker`. The `scan` and `findings.jq` sketches below were run against trufflehog 3.100.0 (Homebrew), under both bash-as-`sh` and `dash`, on a scratch tree built at run time. They gave byte-identical output, the planted values appeared nowhere in stdout or stderr, no temp dir was left behind, `^vendor/` was excluded, and the fingerprint matched an independent Python computation.\n\n### Summary\n\n- Add one starter role directory, `internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/`, with `scan`, `findings.jq`, `Dockerfile` and `exclude-paths`. `allow` is supported but not shipped.\n- Add the starter override line, `route: needs-human` included (it moves here from #217, owner decision), and the `ard init` PR-body opt-out note.\n- Add the do-not-re-route sentence and the human runbook to the fixed issue body, with a test.\n- Record the AGPL-3.0 licence in the role's docs and Dockerfile header; the binary is not added to the root `Dockerfile` or the published `ard` image.\n- Update the starter-tree listings in `internal/roles` and `internal/initcmd` tests.\n- Add unit tests with a fake `trufflehog`: the canary test (including a run killed mid-stream), fail-closed cases, the fingerprint golden, aggregation, determinism, output validity, argv, `exclude-paths`, `allow`, missing tools and a static Dockerfile check.\n- Update the proposal's Scanners section and the CLAUDE.md `internal/roles` line.\n- The real-binary integration test and the Docker integration test stay in #217. There is no root `Dockerfile` pin: TruffleHog is AGPL-3.0 and stays out of the published image.\n\n**Size: L (about 850 changed lines; budget below). Risk: medium-high.** This code handles live secrets, and a projection bug publishes one in a public issue. A human should read `scan` and `findings.jq` line by line before merge.\n\n### Tech lead\n\n**Architecture fit.** The role has the same shape as `scanners/cve`:\n- `scan` runs with cwd set to the read-only worktree at the tick's SHA.\n- It finds its sibling files from its own path.\n- It prints findings only as its last action, and exits 0, 1 or 2 (2 means a missing tool).\n- It writes only to a `mktemp -d` that is removed on exit.\n\nNo Go code outside tests changes. The controller pipeline, executor and config are untouched: #215 owns `route:` and the pre-filing guard.\n\n**The embed makes wiring automatic, so the override must ship with the role (Q1).** `roles.go` embeds the whole `scanners` directory (`//go:embed config.yaml reviewers scanners triage workers`). Adding `internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/` therefore puts it in `roles.FS`, and `ard init` proposes it from the moment this PR merges. It also breaks `TestFSContents` and initcmd's `starterTree` unless those listings change here. Without the override line, an adopter would get the role with defaults:\n- `route: pending`, so leaked-credential issues go to agent triage, which is exactly what owner decision 4 forbids;\n- `every: 4h`, `group_size: 10`.\n\nSo this PR must also carry:\n- the `config.yaml` override with `route: needs-human`;\n- the listing tests;\n- the `roles.go` comment.\n\n#217 shrinks to the integration tests, the Docker integration test and CLAUDE.md. Its body is edited to match (done, owner decision 2026-11-23).\n\n**Dependencies.**\n- **#215 (hard).** `config.LoadFS` rejects an unknown override key, so the starter `config.yaml` line `route: needs-human` fails `TestEmbedded*`, `TestInitOpensPR` and `ard config check` until #215 is on `main`. ard's worker should answer `blocked` until then.\n  - **What this plan assumes from #215:**\n    - `overrides.scanners/<name>.route` accepts `pending`, `none` or `needs-human` on scanner roles only (deterministic scanners default to `pending`);\n    - `config.Role` exposes it, for example as `Route` with constants such as `config.RoutePending` and `config.RouteNeedsHuman`;\n    - the guard runs `redact.Builtin()`, plus gitleaks when enabled, over the decoded fields of each finding (title, body, files, fingerprint, group) and the known-value check, always on, and fails the run closed with the existing `scan_failed` outcome.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2560c54e-5401-43d4-a863-1441d1a300ef","uuid":"07a98467-a292-4bcf-953b-c9894785162c","timestamp":"2026-11-23T19:32:19.938Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"618:----\n624:----\n625:== .ard/triage/engineer/prompt.txt\n631:== .ard/triage/lead/prompt.txt\n637:== .ard/workers/engineer/prompt.txt\n643:== .ard/reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\n- **Issue body, fixed text** (a test asserts it): treat the credential as leaked and rotate it first; do not add `ard:pending` before the credential is rotated, because triage and worker agents would read the file; and the human runbook (rotate first, remove the value from HEAD, do not close while the secret is still at HEAD, false positives, the cap, history is not rewritten).\n- **Licence:** TruffleHog is AGPL-3.0. It s